From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sf2000 linux port <sf2000@local>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 06:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: use only relocated HI16 pairs

The MIPS bFLT loader scans backward from a LO16 relocation to find a matching
LUI when the relocation stream is not perfectly adjacent. That scan was also
accepting ordinary non-relocated constants, such as a nearby lui v0,0x3500.
The 0095 hardware log showed that false match producing 0x350076ec for a
BusyBox LO16 relocation.

Keep the scan, but only accept LUI instructions that have already been seen in
the relocation stream as real HI16 relocations. If no relocated HI16 is known,
leave the LO16 as an orphan low-half relocation instead of pairing it with an
unrelated constant and later patching that constant as if it were a symbol
high half.
---
 arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h | 6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h b/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
--- a/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
+++ b/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
@@ -98,12 +98,10 @@ static inline int flat_mips_find_hi16_for_lo16(u32 __user *rp, u32 lo,
 		if ((insn & 0xffe00000) != 0x3c000000 ||
 		    flat_mips_lui_rt(insn) != rs)
 			continue;
+		if (!flat_mips_lookup_hi16((__force u32 __user *)scan, hi_insn))
+			continue;
 
 		*hi_rp = (__force u32 __user *)scan;
-		if (!flat_mips_lookup_hi16(*hi_rp, hi_insn)) {
-			*hi_insn = insn;
-			flat_mips_remember_hi16(*hi_rp, insn);
-		}
 		return 1;
 	}
 
